% Goal

Implement and maintain `brain/api/api_stems.py`. ROUTES registered by playlist_editor.make_handler: GET /api/stems (?kind=vocals|instrumentals&q=&refresh=1) -> PlaylistApp.stem_list (rows cached for a minute, cleared on an override); POST /api/stems/kind {track_id, kind} -> set_stem_kind (global note; the in-memory Track is updated so Curate's badge follows); GET /api/stems/beds?vocal_id= -> ranked beds; GET/POST /api/stems/layer -> status / start_stem_layer (only from a button press; refuses with 409 while a full mix or an audition plays, or for an odd count shift; dry_run plans without Mixxx); POST /api/stems/layer/stop. Uses the same control-port precedence as auditions.

Human story: `user_stories/story__when_i_pick_a_vocal_and_an_instrumental_mixxx_plays_them_together_live.md`; it extends `user_stories/story__when_i_add_vocals_only_and_instrumental_only_tracks_i_layer_them_i_do_not_play_the_acapella_in_full.md`, whose rules (never a dry acapella, the bed stays live, Get Up over Outta Control is the canonical layer) still hold.

% Product contract

- Preserve the exact public interface declared in `<pdd-interface>`.
- Treat the reviewed architecture description in this prompt as normative behavior.
- Preserve compatible behavior outside this module's stated responsibility; do not redesign unrelated mixing or playback logic.
- Nothing in this module renders audio; Mixxx plays the original files live.
- Target Python 3.13+.
- Inspect the current implementation, its declared dependency modules, and the focused tests (`tests/test_stem_layer.py`, `tests/test_stems.py`) before changing code. This is a brownfield source prompt: working, tested behavior not contradicted here remains part of the contract.

% Architecture detail

ROUTES registered by playlist_editor.make_handler: GET /api/stems (?kind=vocals|instrumentals&q=&refresh=1) -> PlaylistApp.stem_list (rows cached for a minute, cleared on an override); POST /api/stems/kind {track_id, kind} -> set_stem_kind (global note; the in-memory Track is updated so Curate's badge follows); GET /api/stems/beds?vocal_id= -> ranked beds; GET/POST /api/stems/layer -> status / start_stem_layer (only from a button press; refuses with 409 while a full mix or an audition plays, or for an odd count shift; dry_run plans without Mixxx); POST /api/stems/layer/stop. Uses the same control-port precedence as auditions.
